{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/141527-pact-duration-aspects","id":141527,"title":"Pact Duration Aspects","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Demon: The Descent"],"posts":[{"date":"2014-05-18T06:54:52-07:00","id":141527,"title":"Pact Duration Aspects","content":"Hey, <br /> <br /> How exactly do pact duration aspects work? In the book it is said that they are on the side of Demon's benefits. How does this work? How to the aspects work in different cases? Could you explain the cases of:<br /> A) Durations of the benefits are equal on both sides. (Permanent for both)<br /> B) Duration is longer for the demon (Demon Permanently takes a part of his life, for a week of riches to the mortal)<br /> C) Duration is longer for the mortal (Demon takes a part of his life for a month, but the mortal stays rich for a year). <br /> <br /> 1) Do all the Aspects go on demons side? So it would be A) 6 points on demons side B) 3 on demon (3 for permanent, 0 for week) C) 3 on demon (1 for month, 2 for year)<br /> 2) Or should it be that the benefactor of it pays? So A) 3 points on each side. B) 3 On Demons side 0 On mortals side. C) 1 for Demon, 2 for Mortal. <br /> <br /> As written it seems like like 1) is correct.. however I somehow feel that 2) should be correct (or perhaps the intention?)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T21:12:59-07:00","id":142061,"title":"","content":"Pact duration gets figured once (as in, it always lasts the same length for both parties) and it is paid for by the demon.<br /> <br /> <br /> Mortals can gain the following benefits:<br /> Assets (1 to 3 each), Skill (1 to 3 each)<br /> <br /> Demons can gain the following:<br /> Cover (1 to 3), Cult (2 to 5), Soul (3)<br /> <br /> Duration (1 to 3) is also added to the Demon's side of the bargain. Soul Pacts have to be permanent (3), as one of my players discovered after a hastily written pact last night.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2630-mayberry","name":"Mayberry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2630_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-18T22:47:37-07:00","id":142102,"title":"","content":"But.. even the book mentions pacts of different length on the sides.. the book said &quot; It is all too easy to convince a chronic gambler to gain fantastic wealth for one day in exchange for giving up his wife for a year \u2026 or forever.&quot;<br /> <br /> So it should be possible. And it's also appropriate to be able to do so. Anyways, if as written, they are always the same, then I'd like to listen on opinions on how could it be enabled...","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T14:20:42-07:00","id":142671,"title":"","content":"You're absolutely correct. So, the easiest answer would be: Demon pays for the longest Duration, once. On the other hand, screwing over a mortal could be said to be to the demon's benefit, and Pacts are exceptionally cheap, so adding another penalty to the demon's side of the equation seems perfectly fair.<br /> <br /> So, if a mortal gains a benefit of becoming a famous racecar driver for a month (1) while the Demon gains his firstborn son permanently (3), I'd probably charge him 4 rather than 3. But, we know from the examples in the book, at least, that you don't pay twice for matching Durations.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2630-mayberry","name":"Mayberry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2630_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T14:50:08-07:00","id":142686,"title":"","content":"But given that example, isn't it to the mortal's benefit that he's a racecar driver for a month, instead of a week(where the cost would be 0)? Same way, if the mortal is to have longer duration (permanent) isn't it fair that he's the one paying (so two more on duration for the racecar driver example).","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:30:07-07:00","id":142721,"title":"","content":"The written examples in the book, on pg 194, both of them, have them Demon paying the Duration aspect, one time. If that doesn't work for you, then you can do something else in your games.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2630-mayberry","name":"Mayberry","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2630_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2014-05-19T15:59:13-07:00","id":142732,"title":"","content":"Alright. Then let's shift this discussion towards possible changes/houserules to this. Does anyone use any changes to the pact duration rules? If so, what are they? If not, what do you think of these possible variants:<br /> a) Demon pays for the longest duration, however the other one may be shorter than that.<br /> b) Each sides pay for their own duration, because they benefit from it<br /> c) magic?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"https://drive.google.com/drive/folders/0B5_EJSgV1u4SOFFJc3M5VmFDWVk?resourcekey=0-GEErNnDbGqlKYgoiuGausw&amp;usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My Bloodline conversions</a><br /> <a href=\"https://docs.google.com/document/d/1IbeKfqhWuG8jPN9vpGmDo0VY9n9-4ejxvRzfJRoir4k/edit?usp=sharing\" target=\"_blank\">My House rules</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/294-griautis","name":"Griautis","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar294_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2293"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}